01:04:03,529 --> 01:04:09,529
The Anderson Tapes is a 1971 American crime film directed by Sidney Lumet and starring Sean Connery and
featuring Dyan Cannon, Martin Balsam, Ralph Meeker, Garrett Morris, Margaret Hamilton, and Alan King.

12
01:09:52,941 --> 01:09:58,941
The screenplay by Frank Pierson was based on the 1970 epistolary novel of the same name by
Lawrence Sanders, which consists primarily of transcripts of tape recordings.

13
01:15:42,352 --> 01:15:48,352
The film is scored by Quincy Jones and marks the
feature film debut of Christopher Walken.

14
01:21:31,764 --> 01:21:37,764
It was the first major film to focus on the pervasiveness of electronic surveillance,
from security cameras in public places to hidden recording devices.

15
01:27:21,176 --> 01:27:27,176
The film explores themes of new york city, robbery, based on
novel or book, internal affairs, surveillance.

